CMPT 276 Project - Phase 1, Part 2
Group 25

Primary Actor: User/Player

Scenario:
1.     The “Start” screen is displayed to User
2.     User presses the play button
3.     User will read instructions
4.     User presses “Start” button to start playing game
5.     The system displays the maze with User’s character as a car
6.     The timer will start at 0, counting upwards
7.     The progression bar will start empty
8.     Points counter will start at 0
9.     User will press UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT (W,A,S,D) key to move the main character (car)
10.    The User moves the main character to collect coins (10 coins in total) (coins disappear from cell after being caught and add +5 points to the score and +1 to the progression bar)
11.    User will avoid being caught by the Concord officer by moving UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT using the corresponding keys on keyboard (W,A,S,D)
12.    The User collects lost student notes and gains 10 more points towards final score, the lost notes will disappear from cell
12.    The User collects all 10 coins in the maze
13.    The “You Win” screen is displayed to the User showing the final score and time
14.    User presses the “Play Again” button to play again
 
Exceptions:
1.     User Presses the “Quit” button to quit playing the game – “Start” screen (beginning screen) should be displayed to User
2.     User tries to move the main character into a wall – main character should not be able to move into a wall, and will remain in its current cell
3.     User tries to move the main character into a traffic cone– main character should not be able to move into the traffic cone, and will remain in its current cell
4.     User is caught by the Concord officer – “Game Over” screen should be displayed with the option for User to either play again or quit playing by pressing the corresponding buttons
5.     User moves main character into a parked car – 8 points will be deducted from their score, if the User finishes the game successfully
6.     User does not collect the lost notes in time and the lost notes disappears – User will not gain 10 bonus points towards the final score
8.     Concord officer runs into a parked car, coin, or lost notes – the reward/punishment is not affected and remains on its cell
9.     Concord officer tries to move into the wall or the traffic cones – Concord officer remains in its current cell
10.    User loses enough points such that their score is a negative value (negative amount of points) – “Game Over” screen is displayed with the option for User to either play again or quit playing by pressing the corresponding buttons
11.    User does not press a button on keyboard (or does not press a valid button on keyboard) – main character will not move
 

